        "answer": {
          "short": "Missing entries, by column from left to right: $a=3$, $b=\\pm2$, $a=3$.\n\nThe answer book gives $b=2$, selecting the positive root.",
          "worked": "Using $c=2ab^2$, the second column gives\n$$\\begin{align*}24&=2a\\times2^2\\\\a&=\\frac{24}{8}\\\\a&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe third column gives\n$$\\begin{align*}48&=2\\times6\\times b^2\\\\b^2&=4\\\\b&=\\pm2.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth signs give $b^2=4$. The answer book selects $b=2$.\n\nThe fourth column gives\n$$\\begin{align*}54&=2a\\times3^2\\\\a&=\\frac{54}{18}\\\\a&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
